<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S4.T2.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Comparison on <span id="S4.T2.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MATHVERSE</span> (<span id="S4.T2.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">testmini</span>).</span> We report category-wise results: Text-Dominant (TD), <span id="S4.T2.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Vision-Intensive</span> (VI, requiring complex visual reasoning), <span id="S4.T2.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Vision-Dominant</span> (VD, where visual information prevails), and <span id="S4.T2.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Vision-Only</span> (VO, without text prompts). Results are averaged in the ALL column. We contrast these visually grounded categories (VI, VD, VO) against the TD reference.</figcaption>
