<section id="Pt0.A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix 0.A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="Pt0.A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.A.1 </span>Detailed Statistics and Split Information</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report detailed statistics for the evaluation benchmarks used in this work, including <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MathVerse</span> and <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoAux</span>.</p>
</div>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MathVerse</span>.</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate on the <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MathVerse</span> <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">testmini</span> split, which comprises four categories: <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TD</span>, <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VI</span>, <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VD</span>, and <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VO</span>. Each category contains 788 test instances, resulting in a total of 3,152 test samples.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoAux</span>.</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further assess the model’s robustness in <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Visually-Dependent Geometric Reasoning</span>, we curated <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoAux</span>, a diagnostic evaluation suite specifically designed for problems that cannot be solved through direct image-to-text translation. These instances represent a challenging problem scope where the solution remains unreachable through initial visual data alone; instead, the model must introduce external geometric elements—such as auxiliary lines, rotations, or transformations—to bridge the logic gap and complete the reasoning chain.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.T4" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.T4.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Distribution and taxonomy of the <span id="Pt0.A1.T4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoAux</span> benchmark.</span> Left: taxonomy counts. Right: pie chart. Visual-operation labels are non-exclusive, so their counts may exceed the total number of instances.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
