<p id="Pt0.A1.T4.8" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:172.5pt;"><span id="Pt0.A1.T4.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;position:relative; bottom:-0.1pt;"><img src="2603.12166v1/Geoaux_bing.png" id="Pt0.A1.T4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:238/238;" width="238" height="238" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.12166v1/geoaux_radar.svg" id="Pt0.A1.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/250;" width="452" height="250"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F4.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F4.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Radar visualization on <span id="Pt0.A1.F4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoAux</span>.<span id="Pt0.A1.F4.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Left: accuracy across four <em id="Pt0.A1.F4.8.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">knowledge domains</em>. Right: accuracy across eight <em id="Pt0.A1.F4.8.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">visual operations</em>. Curves are drawn from Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ LatentGeo: Learnable Auxiliary Constructions in Latent Space for Multimodal Geometric Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> for representative baselines and </span>LatentGeo<span id="Pt0.A1.F4.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The construction of <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoAux</span> begins with an LLM-driven synthesis phase, where frontier models are employed to augment existing geometry problems by proposing complex auxiliary constructions and multi-step constraints. This is followed by a rigorous human-in-the-loop refinement and expert assessment to ensure geometric validity, visual clarity, and to verify that each problem effectively evaluates the intrinsic reasoning capabilities of MLLMs. We categorize each instance based on two dimensions: <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Knowledge Domain</span> and <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Visual Operation</span>. The former represents the mathematical field, while the latter specifies the primary spatial reasoning skill required.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The detailed distribution of the <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoAux</span> benchmark is summarized in Table <a href="#Pt0.A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ GeoAux. ‣ 0.A.1 Detailed Statistics and Split Information ‣ Appendix 0.A Appendix ‣ LatentGeo: Learnable Auxiliary Constructions in Latent Space for Multimodal Geometric Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. The dataset comprises a total of 2,228 unique instances, with a heavy emphasis on Euclidean Plane Geometry and Alignment-based operations to reflect real-school geometry challenges.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Representative Benchmark Example.</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present four benchmark exemplars from <span id="Pt0.A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoAux</span>, one for each major knowledge category, to clarify the diversity of auxiliary-construction demands covered by the benchmark.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="596.18" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 480.31 596.18" width="480.31"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,596.18) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#CCD8E2;" fill="#CCD8E2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.98 L 0 592.2 C 0 594.4 1.78 596.18 3.98 596.18 L 476.34 596.18 C 478.53 596.18 480.31 594.4 480.31 592.2 L 480.31 3.98 C 480.31 1.78 478.53 0 476.34 0 L 3.98 0 C 1.78 0 0 1.78 0 3.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F5F8FB;" fill="#F5F8FB" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 3.98 L 0.83 570.07 L 479.48 570.07 L 479.48 3.98 C 479.48 2.24 478.07 0.83 476.34 0.83 L 3.98 0.83 C 2.24 0.83 0.83 2.24 0.83 3.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4F6473;" fill="#4F6473" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 570.9 L 0.83 592.2 C 0.83 593.94 2.24 595.35 3.98 595.35 L 476.34 595.35 C 478.07 595.35 479.48 593.94 479.48 592.2 L 479.48 570.9 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.43 580.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.77em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="425.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:30.77em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#F7F9FB;">Benchmark Example 1</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.43 14.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:35.43em;--ltx-fo-height:39.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="547.98" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 545.56)" width="490.25"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:35.43em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Knowledge.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Euclidean Plane Geometry.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Visual Operation.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Elemental Connectivity.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Hint: Please solve the problem and provide the final boxed answer as the uppercase option letter only, e.g., </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In the figure, lines </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\parallel b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\parallel b</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. In the equilateral triangle </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle ABC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle ABC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, vertex </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> lies on line </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle 1=20^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">20</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle 1=20^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Find the measure of </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle 2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Options: A. </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="60^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">60</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">60^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  B. </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">45</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  C. </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">40</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  D. </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="30^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">30</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">30^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question Image.</span></span><img src="2603.12166v1/geoaux_3.png" id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:190/190;" width="190" height="190" alt="Refer to caption">
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Construction Requirement.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Extend </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to meet line </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and convert the target angle into a solvable relation under the parallel-line constraint.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Correct Answer.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{C}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (</span><math id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">40</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Key Evaluation Focus.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.pic1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> This sample tests whether the model can introduce the missing auxiliary connection needed for angle reasoning, rather than relying on direct visual reading alone.</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Benchmark example from Euclidean Plane Geometry.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F6" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="596.18" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 480.31 596.18" width="480.31"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,596.18) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#CCD8E2;" fill="#CCD8E2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.98 L 0 592.2 C 0 594.4 1.78 596.18 3.98 596.18 L 476.34 596.18 C 478.53 596.18 480.31 594.4 480.31 592.2 L 480.31 3.98 C 480.31 1.78 478.53 0 476.34 0 L 3.98 0 C 1.78 0 0 1.78 0 3.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F5F8FB;" fill="#F5F8FB" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 3.98 L 0.83 570.07 L 479.48 570.07 L 479.48 3.98 C 479.48 2.24 478.07 0.83 476.34 0.83 L 3.98 0.83 C 2.24 0.83 0.83 2.24 0.83 3.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4F6473;" fill="#4F6473" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 570.9 L 0.83 592.2 C 0.83 593.94 2.24 595.35 3.98 595.35 L 476.34 595.35 C 478.07 595.35 479.48 593.94 479.48 592.2 L 479.48 570.9 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.43 580.01)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.77em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="425.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:30.77em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#F7F9FB;">Benchmark Example 2</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.43 14.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:35.43em;--ltx-fo-height:39.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="547.98" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 545.56)" width="490.25"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:35.43em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Knowledge.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Spatial &amp; Projective Geometry.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Visual Operation.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Orthogonal &amp; Parallel Alignment; Elemental Connectivity; Structural Partitioning.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Hint: Please solve the problem and provide the final boxed answer as an exact angle measure, keeping degree notation if needed, e.g., </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">50</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∘</mo></msup></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In the cube </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABCD{-}A_{1}B_{1}C_{1}D_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABCD{-}A_{1}B_{1}C_{1}D_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with edge length </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, find the angle between the line </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and the plane </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}B_{1}BD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}B_{1}BD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question Image.</span></span><img src="2603.12166v1/geoaux_1010.png" id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:190/190;" width="190" height="190" alt="Refer to caption">
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Construction Requirement.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Introduce the top-face center via diagonal intersection and identify the foot of the perpendicular from </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to plane </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}B_{1}BD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}B_{1}BD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Correct Answer.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{30^{\circ}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">30</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∘</mo></msup></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{30^{\circ}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Key Evaluation Focus.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.pic1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> This case probes whether the model can decompose a 3D angle-to-plane problem into an auxiliary planar configuration through orthogonality and structural partitioning.</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Benchmark example from Spatial &amp; Projective Geometry.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
