<span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Knowledge.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Analytic Coordinate Geometry.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Visual Operation.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Elemental Connectivity.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Hint: Please solve the problem and provide the final boxed answer as the uppercase option letter only, e.g., </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In the figure, quadrilateral </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="OABC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OABC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a rhombus. Line </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is perpendicular to the </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-axis with foot </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The graph of </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\dfrac{4}{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">x</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\dfrac{4}{x}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> passes through </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and intersects </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> at </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Given </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="OD=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OD=2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, what is the area of </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle OCE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle OCE</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">?</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Options: A. </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.16" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  B. </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.17" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  C. </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\sqrt{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.1.18" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  D. </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\sqrt{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question Image.</span></span><img src="2603.12166v1/geoaux_1353.png" id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:190/190;" width="190" height="190" alt="Refer to caption">
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Construction Requirement.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Connect </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and combine the conic constraint with the rhombus side-equality relation to recover the geometry needed for the area computation.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Correct Answer.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{C}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (</span><math id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\sqrt{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Key Evaluation Focus.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.pic1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> This sample tests whether the model can bridge symbolic curve information and geometric structure by adding a non-explicit segment that stabilizes the area reasoning.</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Benchmark example from Analytic Coordinate Geometry.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F8" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="612.79" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 480.31 612.79" width="480.31"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,612.79) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#CCD8E2;" fill="#CCD8E2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.98 L 0 608.81 C 0 611 1.78 612.79 3.98 612.79 L 476.34 612.79 C 478.53 612.79 480.31 611 480.31 608.81 L 480.31 3.98 C 480.31 1.78 478.53 0 476.34 0 L 3.98 0 C 1.78 0 0 1.78 0 3.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F5F8FB;" fill="#F5F8FB" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 3.98 L 0.83 586.67 L 479.48 586.67 L 479.48 3.98 C 479.48 2.24 478.07 0.83 476.34 0.83 L 3.98 0.83 C 2.24 0.83 0.83 2.24 0.83 3.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4F6473;" fill="#4F6473" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 587.5 L 0.83 608.81 C 0.83 610.54 2.24 611.96 3.98 611.96 L 476.34 611.96 C 478.07 611.96 479.48 610.54 479.48 608.81 L 479.48 587.5 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.43 596.61)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.77em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="425.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:30.77em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#F7F9FB;">Benchmark Example 4</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.43 14.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:35.43em;--ltx-fo-height:40.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="564.59" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 562.16)" width="490.25"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:35.43em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Knowledge.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Functional Graph Geometry.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Visual Operation.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Analytic Overlay.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Hint: Please solve the problem and provide the final boxed answer as the uppercase option letter only, e.g., </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">As shown, a bridge arch is modeled by a parabola. The maximum height is 16 meters, and the span is 40 meters. On segment </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, at a point 5 meters from the center </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, what is the height of the bridge (in meters)?</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Options: A. </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">14</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">14</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  B. </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  C. </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">13</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">13</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  D. </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question Image.</span></span><img src="2603.12166v1/geoaux_1633.png" id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:190/190;" width="190" height="190" alt="Refer to caption">
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Construction Requirement.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Overlay an analytic coordinate system by taking the bridge span as the </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-axis and the midpoint as the origin, then recover the parabola from its vertex and intercepts.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Correct Answer.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{B}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (</span><math id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Key Evaluation Focus.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.pic1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> This sample examines whether the model can translate a real-scene functional graph into an analytic form before performing numeric evaluation.</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Benchmark example from Functional Graph Geometry.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.A.2 </span>Hyperparameters</h3>

<section id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SFT Hyperparameters.</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We fine-tune the model using a multi-stage supervised fine-tuning (SFT) strategy. The learning rate follows a cosine decay schedule, and mixed precision with <span id="Pt0.A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bfloat16</span> is employed to optimize training efficiency. The detailed hyperparameters for each SFT stage are summarized in Table <a href="#Pt0.A1.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ SFT Hyperparameters. ‣ 0.A.2 Hyperparameters ‣ Appendix 0.A Appendix ‣ LatentGeo: Learnable Auxiliary Constructions in Latent Space for Multimodal Geometric Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
