<section id="Pt0.A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.A.3 </span>Prompting Scheme</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt one unified prompt for SFT/RL/inference and a two-stage evaluation protocol (answer extraction, then answer judging). We report the three prompt templates below.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F9" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Pt0.A1.F9.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="182.75" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 480.31 182.75" width="480.31"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,182.75) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.94 L 0 178.81 C 0 180.98 1.76 182.75 3.94 182.75 L 476.38 182.75 C 478.55 182.75 480.31 180.98 480.31 178.81 L 480.31 3.94 C 480.31 1.76 478.55 0 476.38 0 L 3.94 0 C 1.76 0 0 1.76 0 3.94 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.94 L 0 161.04 L 480.31 161.04 L 480.31 3.94 C 480.31 1.76 478.55 0 476.38 0 L 3.94 0 C 1.76 0 0 1.76 0 3.94 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 7.87 168.43)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.57em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="464.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F9.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.57em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F9.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F9.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt: Geometry Reasoning Instruction (SFT &amp; RL)</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 7.87 143.82)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.29em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:9.83em;font-size:10pt;" height="145.29" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.34)" width="502.15"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F9.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.29em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F9.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F9.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[Image]
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F9.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">You are a helpful assistant.
<br class="ltx_break">First, analyze the problem with the image and describe all necessary geometric constructions or spatial operations using concise and standard language.
<br class="ltx_break">Then, provide a reasoning to solve the problem.
<br class="ltx_break">Finally, give the final answer. The final answer must be boxed, e.g., \boxed{answer}.
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:2.8pt;">
</span>Question:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F9.pic1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">{question}</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Unified instruction prompt used for SFT, RL, and inference.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F10" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Pt0.A1.F10.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="227.22" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 480.31 227.22" width="480.31"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,227.22) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.94 L 0 223.28 C 0 225.46 1.76 227.22 3.94 227.22 L 476.38 227.22 C 478.55 227.22 480.31 225.46 480.31 223.28 L 480.31 3.94 C 480.31 1.76 478.55 0 476.38 0 L 3.94 0 C 1.76 0 0 1.76 0 3.94 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.94 L 0 207.04 L 480.31 207.04 L 480.31 3.94 C 480.31 1.76 478.55 0 476.38 0 L 3.94 0 C 1.76 0 0 1.76 0 3.94 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 7.87 213.67)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.57em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="464.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F10.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.57em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F10.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F10.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt: Answer Extraction for Evaluation</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 7.87 190.52)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.29em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:13.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="191.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="502.15"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F10.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.29em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F10.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F10.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">{DEMO_PROMPT}
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F10.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">(Contains extraction guidelines and in-context examples.)
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:2.8pt;">
</span>{hint}
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F10.pic1.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">Hint: This is a Multiple Choice Question. Extract only the option letter (A, B, C, D); if the model outputs option content, map it back to the corresponding letter when possible.
<br class="ltx_break">Hint: This is a Free-form Question. Extract the final value or expression.
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:2.8pt;">
</span>Question:<span id="Pt0.A1.F10.pic1.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> {query}
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Model response:<span id="Pt0.A1.F10.pic1.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> {response}
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Extracted answer:<span id="Pt0.A1.F10.pic1.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Answer-extraction template used before final matching.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F11" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Pt0.A1.F11.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="179.83" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 480.31 179.83" width="480.31"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,179.83) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.94 L 0 175.89 C 0 178.06 1.76 179.83 3.94 179.83 L 476.38 179.83 C 478.55 179.83 480.31 178.06 480.31 175.89 L 480.31 3.94 C 480.31 1.76 478.55 0 476.38 0 L 3.94 0 C 1.76 0 0 1.76 0 3.94 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.94 L 0 159.65 L 480.31 159.65 L 480.31 3.94 C 480.31 1.76 478.55 0 476.38 0 L 3.94 0 C 1.76 0 0 1.76 0 3.94 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 7.87 166.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:33.57em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="464.51"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F11.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:33.57em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F11.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F11.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt: Equivalence-Based Answer Judging</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 7.87 143.13)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.29em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:9.78em;font-size:10pt;" height="143.91" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="502.15"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F11.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.29em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F11.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F11.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">You are a math teacher grading a student’s answer.
<br class="ltx_break">Question: {question}
<br class="ltx_break">Correct Answer: {ground_truth}
<br class="ltx_break">Student Answer: {prediction}
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:2.8pt;">
Does the student answer match the correct answer?
<br class="ltx_break">For numerical answers, they should be equivalent (e.g., 1.5 equals 3/2).
<br class="ltx_break">For multiple choice, the option letter should match.
<br class="ltx_break">For expressions, they should be algebraically equivalent.
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:2.8pt;">
Reply only with “True” or “False”.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Judge prompt used for final correctness decision.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.A.4 </span>Training Data Sources</h3>

<section id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SFT Training Data.</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We construct a high-quality Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT) dataset comprising approximately 30,000 geometry problems. These samples are aggregated from multiple public geometric reasoning benchmarks, including <span id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MathCanvas</span>, <span id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Geometry3K</span>, <span id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoQA+</span>, <span id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GEOS</span>, and <span id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">UniGeo</span>.
To ensure the data quality and alignment with our training objective, we employ a rigorous data processing pipeline involving both manual curation and LLM-assisted reformatting.
Specifically, raw data instances are first manually filtered to exclude low-quality images or ambiguous problem statements. Subsequently, we utilize advanced LLMs (e.g., GPT-4o) to canonicalize the solution traces into the unified format required for SFT (as detailed in Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A1.SS3" title="0.A.3 Prompting Scheme ‣ Appendix 0.A Appendix ‣ LatentGeo: Learnable Auxiliary Constructions in Latent Space for Multimodal Geometric Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.A.3</span></a>), ensuring a consistent structure of visual description, reasoning steps, and the final boxed answer.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F12" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="710.06" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 480.31 710.06" width="480.31"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,710.06) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#CCD8E2;" fill="#CCD8E2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.98 L 0 706.08 C 0 708.28 1.78 710.06 3.98 710.06 L 476.34 710.06 C 478.53 710.06 480.31 708.28 480.31 706.08 L 480.31 3.98 C 480.31 1.78 478.53 0 476.34 0 L 3.98 0 C 1.78 0 0 1.78 0 3.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F5F8FB;" fill="#F5F8FB" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 3.98 L 0.83 683.94 L 479.48 683.94 L 479.48 3.98 C 479.48 2.24 478.07 0.83 476.34 0.83 L 3.98 0.83 C 2.24 0.83 0.83 2.24 0.83 3.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4F6473;" fill="#4F6473" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 684.77 L 0.83 706.08 C 0.83 707.82 2.24 709.23 3.98 709.23 L 476.34 709.23 C 478.07 709.23 479.48 707.82 479.48 706.08 L 479.48 684.77 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.43 693.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.77em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="425.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:30.77em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#F7F9FB;">Representative SFT Training Example</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.43 11.85)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:38.55em;--ltx-fo-height:47.83em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="661.86" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 661.86)" width="533.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:38.55em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> In square </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABCD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABCD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with side length </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, the angle bisector of </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle DAC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle DAC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> intersects </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> at </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Points </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> move on </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, respectively. Find the minimum value of </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DQ+PQ" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">Q</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">Q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DQ+PQ</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question Image.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p6" class="ltx_para"><img src="2603.12166v1/ques_img.png" id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:145/145;" width="145" height="145" alt="Refer to caption">
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Assistant Output.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Reflect </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> across line </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to point </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Since </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> lies on </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, convert </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DQ+PQ" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">Q</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">Q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DQ+PQ</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> into the broken path </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}Q+QP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">Q</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">P</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}Q+QP</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, then reduce the minimization to the distance from </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to line </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Let </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> be the foot of the perpendicular from </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.800em">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p3.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;|latent_start|&gt;&lt;|latent_pad|&gt;…&lt;|latent_pad|&gt;&lt;|latent_end|&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Because <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> lies on the mirror line <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE</annotation></semantics></math>, reflection gives <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DQ=D^{\prime}Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DQ=D^{\prime}Q</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DQ+PQ=D^{\prime}Q+QP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DQ+PQ=D^{\prime}Q+QP</annotation></semantics></math>. For any point <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in AD</annotation></semantics></math>, the broken path from <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> through <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is at least the straight-line distance <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}P</annotation></semantics></math>, with equality when <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime},Q,P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime},Q,P</annotation></semantics></math> are collinear. Therefore, the problem reduces to minimizing <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}P</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> on line segment <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">This minimum is attained when <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, the foot of the perpendicular from <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min(DQ+PQ)=D^{\prime}P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min(DQ+PQ)=D^{\prime}P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE</annotation></semantics></math> bisects <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle DAC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle DAC</annotation></semantics></math>, reflecting ray <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math> across <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AE</annotation></semantics></math> maps it to ray <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> lies on <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD^{\prime}=AD=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD^{\prime}=AD=2</annotation></semantics></math>. In a square, diagonal <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AC</annotation></semantics></math> makes a <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">45</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> angle with side <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle D^{\prime}AP^{\prime}=45^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">45</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle D^{\prime}AP^{\prime}=45^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle AD^{\prime}P^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle AD^{\prime}P^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">45</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">45</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="90^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">90</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">90^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> right triangle with hypotenuse <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AD^{\prime}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AD^{\prime}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, giving <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}P^{\prime}=\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{2}}=\sqrt{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}P^{\prime}=\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{2}}=\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the minimum value is <math id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{\sqrt{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msqrt></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{\sqrt{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Auxiliary Image.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.p8" class="ltx_para"><img src="2603.12166v1/solution_img.png" id="Pt0.A1.F12.pic1.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:136/136;" width="136" height="136" alt="Refer to caption">
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F12.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Representative SFT training example.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data Composition.</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The SFT dataset integrates diverse geometric challenges from the following sources:</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Pt0.A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="Pt0.A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">MathCanvas</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>: A multimodal dataset emphasizing intrinsic visual reasoning. We select instances that require detailed visual understanding to complement text-based logic.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">Geometry3K</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>: A comprehensive benchmark of high-school geometry problems. We utilize its rich annotations to construct step-by-step reasoning chains.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoQA+</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>: A large-scale geometric question-answering dataset. We filter for problems that involve complex calculation and theorem application.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">GEOS</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>: One of the pioneering datasets for geometry problem solving, providing fundamental plane geometry instances.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">UniGeo</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>: A unified geometric reasoning dataset covering both calculation and proof problems across various difficulty levels.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">RL Training Data.</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our RL training data are sampled from three public geometry problem-solving datasets: Geometry3K, GeomVerse, and MathCanvas <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>.
In total, we collect 3,339 problems, including 1,362 from Geometry3K, 1,309 from GeomVerse, and 668 from MathCanvas.
For RL, we use each problem (with its associated diagram/image when provided) as the prompt, and treat the dataset-provided final answer as outcome supervision for reward computation.
Importantly, we do not consume intermediate solution traces (e.g., chain-of-thought or step annotations) as supervision in the RL stage.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data Composition.</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The RL dataset draws from the following sources:</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Pt0.A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="Pt0.A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">Geometry3K</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>: A benchmark of 3,002 high-school geometry multiple-choice problems. We randomly sample 1,362 instances and use the ground-truth answer option as the outcome-based reward signal.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">GeomVerse</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>: A procedurally generated geometry dataset designed to probe reasoning capabilities under controllable factors such as reasoning depth. We sample 1,309 problems and use only their final answers for outcome supervision.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Pt0.A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps">MathCanvas</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>: A multimodal mathematical reasoning resource emphasizing intrinsic visual reasoning and diagram-centric problem solving. We sample 668 geometry instances and use only the dataset-provided final answers as RL reward supervision.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.A.5 </span>RL Training</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Hyperparameters are provided in Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A1.SS2" title="0.A.2 Hyperparameters ‣ Appendix 0.A Appendix ‣ LatentGeo: Learnable Auxiliary Constructions in Latent Space for Multimodal Geometric Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.A.2</span></a>. We include RL training trend figures in this section to visualize reward evolution during policy optimization.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F13" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2603.12166v1/rlall.png" id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/253;" width="476" height="253" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Overall trends</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2603.12166v1/rllatent.png" id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/253;" width="476" height="253" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Latent-related trends</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2603.12166v1/rllength.png" id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/253;" width="476" height="253" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Length-related trends</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2603.12166v1/rlrepetition.png" id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/253;" width="476" height="253" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(d)</span> </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F13.sf4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Repetition-related trends</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F13.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 13</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F13.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">RL training trends.<span id="Pt0.A1.F13.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We report four perspectives of RL optimization: overall behavior, latent-token dynamics, length control, and repetition control.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.A.6 </span>Baselines</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate <span id="Pt0.A1.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LatentGeo</span> on <span id="Pt0.A1.SS6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MATHVERSE</span> (<span id="Pt0.A1.SS6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">testmini</span>) following the model selection in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ LatentGeo: Learnable Auxiliary Constructions in Latent Space for Multimodal Geometric Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. We include Random and Human references, and three groups of model baselines. For <span id="Pt0.A1.SS6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Closed-Source MLLMs</span>, we include GPT-4o <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>, Gemini-1.5-Pro <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>, and Qwen-VL-Plus <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>. For <span id="Pt0.A1.SS6.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Open-Source General MLLMs</span>, we benchmark mPLUG-Owl2-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite>, LLaVA-1.5-13B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>, SPHINX-V2-13B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, LLaVA-NeXT-34B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, DeepSeek-VL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, InternVL2-8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>, and Qwen2-VL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>. For <span id="Pt0.A1.SS6.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Open-Source Math MLLMs</span>, we compare against Math-LLaVA-13B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>, Math-PUMA-Qwen2-7B and Math-PUMA-DeepSeek-Math <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite>, MAVIS-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite>, InfiMM-Math <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>, and MultiMath-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate <span id="Pt0.A1.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LatentGeo</span> on the proposed <span id="Pt0.A1.SS6.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoAux</span> benchmark using two groups of baselines, as summarized in Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ LatentGeo: Learnable Auxiliary Constructions in Latent Space for Multimodal Geometric Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. For <span id="Pt0.A1.SS6.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Closed-Source MLLMs</span>, we include GPT-4o <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>, Qwen3-VL-Flash <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, and GPT-4o-mini <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>. For <span id="Pt0.A1.SS6.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Open-Source General MLLMs</span>, we benchmark LLaVA-1.6 (Vicuna-7B) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, MMR1-7B-RL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>, OpenMMReasoner-RL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>]</cite>, R1-Onevision-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite>, Qwen2.5-VL-7B and Qwen2.5-VL-32B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, Qwen3-VL-8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, InternVL2-8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>, and InternVL3.5-8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>. All models are evaluated under the same GeoAux protocol and report accuracy (%) over 2,228 instances.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.A.7 </span>Case Study</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present several qualitative inference cases from <span id="Pt0.A1.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoAux</span> to illustrate how <span id="Pt0.A1.SS7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LatentGeo</span> introduces latent auxiliary constructions and completes the downstream geometric reasoning chain.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F14" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="597.71" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 480.31 597.71" width="480.31"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,597.71) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#CCD8E2;" fill="#CCD8E2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.98 L 0 593.73 C 0 595.93 1.78 597.71 3.98 597.71 L 476.34 597.71 C 478.53 597.71 480.31 595.93 480.31 593.73 L 480.31 3.98 C 480.31 1.78 478.53 0 476.34 0 L 3.98 0 C 1.78 0 0 1.78 0 3.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F5F8FB;" fill="#F5F8FB" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 3.98 L 0.83 571.59 L 479.48 571.59 L 479.48 3.98 C 479.48 2.24 478.07 0.83 476.34 0.83 L 3.98 0.83 C 2.24 0.83 0.83 2.24 0.83 3.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4F6473;" fill="#4F6473" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 572.42 L 0.83 593.73 C 0.83 595.47 2.24 596.88 3.98 596.88 L 476.34 596.88 C 478.07 596.88 479.48 595.47 479.48 593.73 L 479.48 572.42 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.43 581.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.77em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="425.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:30.77em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#F7F9FB;">Representative Case Study Example</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.43 11.85)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:35.43em;--ltx-fo-height:39.71em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="549.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 549.51)" width="490.25"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:35.43em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Knowledge.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Euclidean Plane Geometry.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Visual Operation.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Elemental Connectivity.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Hint: Please solve the problem and provide the final boxed answer as an exact angle measure, keeping degree notation if needed, e.g., </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">50</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∘</mo></msup></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In the figure, </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PA</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PB</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> are tangents to circle </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> at points </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, respectively. Point </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> lies on circle </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. If </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle AEB=40^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">40</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle AEB=40^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, find </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle APB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle APB</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p2.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question Image.</span></span><img src="2603.12166v1/geoaux_19.png" id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:154/154;" width="154" height="154" alt="Refer to caption">
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Model Response.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Join </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="OA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OA</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="OB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OB</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Since </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PA</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PB</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> are tangents to circle </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we have </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="OA\perp PA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">⟂</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OA\perp PA</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="OB\perp PB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">⟂</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">OB\perp PB</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, so </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle OAP=\angle OBP=90^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">P</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">90</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle OAP=\angle OBP=90^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p4.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;|latent_start|&gt;&lt;|latent_pad|&gt;…&lt;|latent_pad|&gt;&lt;|latent_end|&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The inscribed angle <math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle AEB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle AEB</annotation></semantics></math> subtends arc <math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math>, so the central angle <math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle AOB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle AOB</annotation></semantics></math> subtending the same arc is twice the inscribed angle:
<math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle AOB=2\angle AEB=2\times 40^{\circ}=80^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">40</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">80</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle AOB=2\angle AEB=2\times 40^{\circ}=80^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In quadrilateral <math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AOPB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AOPB</annotation></semantics></math>, the angles at <math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> are right angles, and the angle at <math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">80</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the remaining angle at <math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\angle APB=360^{\circ}-90^{\circ}-90^{\circ}-80^{\circ}=100^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">360</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">90</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">90</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">80</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\angle APB=360^{\circ}-90^{\circ}-90^{\circ}-80^{\circ}=100^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, the answer is <math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{100}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">100</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{100}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Correct Answer.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{100^{\circ}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">100</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">∘</mo></msup></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{100^{\circ}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.pic1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 14</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F14.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Qualitative case study from <span id="Pt0.A1.F14.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoAux</span>.<span id="Pt0.A1.F14.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> </span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F15" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="630.92" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 480.31 630.92" width="480.31"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,630.92) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#CCD8E2;" fill="#CCD8E2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.98 L 0 626.94 C 0 629.14 1.78 630.92 3.98 630.92 L 476.34 630.92 C 478.53 630.92 480.31 629.14 480.31 626.94 L 480.31 3.98 C 480.31 1.78 478.53 0 476.34 0 L 3.98 0 C 1.78 0 0 1.78 0 3.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F5F8FB;" fill="#F5F8FB" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 3.98 L 0.83 604.8 L 479.48 604.8 L 479.48 3.98 C 479.48 2.24 478.07 0.83 476.34 0.83 L 3.98 0.83 C 2.24 0.83 0.83 2.24 0.83 3.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4F6473;" fill="#4F6473" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 605.63 L 0.83 626.94 C 0.83 628.68 2.24 630.09 3.98 630.09 L 476.34 630.09 C 478.07 630.09 479.48 628.68 479.48 626.94 L 479.48 605.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.43 614.75)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.77em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="425.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:30.77em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#F7F9FB;">Representative Case Study Example</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.43 11.85)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:35.43em;--ltx-fo-height:42.11em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="582.72" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 582.72)" width="490.25"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:35.43em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Knowledge.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Euclidean Plane Geometry.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Visual Operation.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Orthogonal &amp; Parallel Alignment; Elemental Connectivity.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Hint: Please solve the problem and provide the final boxed answer as an exact value only, e.g., </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{24}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">24</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{24}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In trapezoid </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABCD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABCD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="EF" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">EF</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the midline. Segment </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AF" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AF</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is drawn. If the area of </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle AEF" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle AEF</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6\,\text{cm}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">6</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">cm</mtext><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6\,\text{cm}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, find the area of trapezoid </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABCD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABCD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (in </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{cm}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">cm</mtext><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{cm}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question Image.</span></span><img src="2603.12166v1/geoaux_31.png" id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:154/154;" width="154" height="154" alt="Refer to caption">
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Model Response.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Draw </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AG\perp BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">G</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">⟂</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AG\perp BC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> on </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BC</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Since </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="EF" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">EF</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the midline of trapezoid </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABCD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABCD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, the distance between the parallel sides </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CD</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AG" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AG</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and the length of the midline is </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="EF=\tfrac{1}{2}(AB+CD)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">F</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">EF=\tfrac{1}{2}(AB+CD)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Therefore, the area of the trapezoid is </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ABCD}=\tfrac{1}{2}(AB+CD)\cdot AG=EF\cdot AG" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">G</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">F</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">G</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ABCD}=\tfrac{1}{2}(AB+CD)\cdot AG=EF\cdot AG</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p4.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;|latent_start|&gt;&lt;|latent_pad|&gt;…&lt;|latent_pad|&gt;&lt;|latent_end|&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Because <math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="EF\parallel AB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.110em">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">EF\parallel AB</annotation></semantics></math>, the triangles <math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle AEF" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle AEF</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangle ABG" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangle ABG</annotation></semantics></math> are similar with similarity ratio <math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{EF}{AB}=\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{EF}{AB}=\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the area ratio is <math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\tfrac{EF}{AB}\right)^{2}=\tfrac{1}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\tfrac{EF}{AB}\right)^{2}=\tfrac{1}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given <math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\triangle AEF}=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\triangle AEF}=6</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\triangle ABG}=4\times 6=24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\triangle ABG}=4\times 6=24</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{ABCD}=S_{\triangle ABG}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">△</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{ABCD}=S_{\triangle ABG}</annotation></semantics></math> (the area of the trapezoid equals the area of the larger similar triangle with the same height <math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AG" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AG</annotation></semantics></math>), the area of trapezoid <math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABCD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABCD</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">24</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the answer is <math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{24}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">24</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{24}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Correct Answer.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{24}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">24</mn></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{24}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.pic1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 15</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Qualitative case study from <span id="Pt0.A1.F15.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoAux</span>.<span id="Pt0.A1.F15.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> </span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F16" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="697.33" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 480.31 697.33" width="480.31"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,697.33) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#CCD8E2;" fill="#CCD8E2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 3.98 L 0 693.35 C 0 695.55 1.78 697.33 3.98 697.33 L 476.34 697.33 C 478.53 697.33 480.31 695.55 480.31 693.35 L 480.31 3.98 C 480.31 1.78 478.53 0 476.34 0 L 3.98 0 C 1.78 0 0 1.78 0 3.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F5F8FB;" fill="#F5F8FB" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 3.98 L 0.83 671.22 L 479.48 671.22 L 479.48 3.98 C 479.48 2.24 478.07 0.83 476.34 0.83 L 3.98 0.83 C 2.24 0.83 0.83 2.24 0.83 3.98 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#4F6473;" fill="#4F6473" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.83 672.05 L 0.83 693.35 C 0.83 695.09 2.24 696.5 3.98 696.5 L 476.34 696.5 C 478.07 696.5 479.48 695.09 479.48 693.35 L 479.48 672.05 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.43 681.16)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:30.77em;--ltx-fo-height:0.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.07" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.65)" width="425.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:30.77em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#F7F9FB;">Representative Case Study Example</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.43 11.85)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:35.43em;--ltx-fo-height:46.91em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="649.14" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 649.14)" width="490.25"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:35.43em;">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Knowledge.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Spatial &amp; Projective Geometry.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Visual Operation.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Spatial Projection &amp; Unfolding; Elemental Connectivity.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Hint: Please solve the problem and provide the final boxed answer as a simplified expression only, e.g., </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{40\sqrt{5}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">40</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">5</mn></msqrt></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{40\sqrt{5}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A cube gift box has side length 20 cm. A gecko is at vertex </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> on the bottom face, and a mosquito is at vertex </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> on the top face, as shown. The gecko must reach the mosquito within 0.5 minutes, moving along the surfaces of the box. What is the minimum speed the gecko must crawl per minute (in cm/min)? Express your answer in simplest radical form.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Question Image.</span></span><img src="2603.12166v1/geoaux_1021.png" id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:154/154;" width="154" height="154" alt="Refer to caption">
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Model Response.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Consider the net of the cube that unfolds the two faces containing the gecko and the mosquito so that the shortest path on the surfaces becomes a straight line in the net. In the net, the gecko starts at </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> on the bottom face and the mosquito is at </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> on the top face. The straight-line distance between </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> in the net is the hypotenuse of a right triangle with legs </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (since the bottom and top faces are separated by </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> cm and the horizontal distance between the corresponding positions on the two faces is </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p4.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> cm).</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">&lt;|latent_start|&gt;&lt;|latent_pad|&gt;…&lt;|latent_pad|&gt;&lt;|latent_end|&gt;</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Thus the shortest path length is <math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{20^{2}+40^{2}}=\sqrt{400+1600}=\sqrt{2000}=20\sqrt{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">40</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">400</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1600</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2000</mn></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{20^{2}+40^{2}}=\sqrt{400+1600}=\sqrt{2000}=20\sqrt{5}</annotation></semantics></math> cm. The gecko has 0.5 minutes to cover this distance, so the required minimum speed is <math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dfrac{20\sqrt{5}}{0.5}=40\sqrt{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.5</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">40</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dfrac{20\sqrt{5}}{0.5}=40\sqrt{5}</annotation></semantics></math> cm/min. Therefore, the answer is <math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{40\sqrt{5}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">40</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></msqrt></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{40\sqrt{5}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#354C5E;">Correct Answer.</span><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{40\sqrt{5}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">40</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="0.900em">5</mn></msqrt></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{40\sqrt{5}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.pic1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 16</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F16.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Qualitative case study from <span id="Pt0.A1.F16.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">GeoAux</span>.<span id="Pt0.A1.F16.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> </span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
